      "quoted_tweet_id": "1930746459382525996",
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Today, @DHSgov announced cancellation of construction of National Security Cutter (NSC) #11, freeing up $260M in taxpayer funds. The leadership of @POTUS and @Sec_Noem drove a conclusive negotiation with Huntington Ingalls Industries, which will include $135M in needed parts for the @USCG existing fleet of NSCs. Continuing the Coast Guard’s transformation through Force Design 2028, this cancellation will help maximize America’s investment in the Coast Guard while realizing cost savings and ensuring on-time, on-budget acquisitions.\n #ForceDesign2028",
      "text_resolved": "Today, @DHSgov announced cancellation of construction of National Security Cutter (NSC) #11, freeing up $260M in taxpayer funds. The leadership of @POTUS and @Sec_Noem drove a conclusive negotiation with Huntington Ingalls Industries, which will include $135M in needed parts for the @USCG existing fleet of NSCs. Continuing the Coast Guard’s transformation through Force Design 2028, this cancellation will help maximize America’s investment in the Coast Guard while realizing cost savings and ensuring on-time, on-budget acquisitions.\n #ForceDesign2028",
