      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Coast Guard crews around the country work diligently to prevent illegal narcotics from entering the United States.\n\nCoast Guard Cutter Kimball exemplified these operations during a recent patrol from February through April, during which they conducted multiple drug interdictions off the coasts of Mexico and Central and South America. This culminated in Kimball offloading more than $191 million worth of cocaine in April.\n\nAs the Coast Guard continues to surge assets across our southern border and maritime approaches, our crews have been leading the fight against drug cartels and Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCO). The dedicated efforts of Kimball – and men and women across the Coast Guard – are directly impacting the ability of cartels and TCOs to smuggle illicit drugs into our communities. \n\n📷PA3 Avery Tibbets & MST3 Austin Wiley\n\n@DHSgov @USCGPACAREA @USCGHawaiiPac \n\n#USCG #USCGHawaii #IndoPacific #druginterdiction",
      "text_resolved": "Coast Guard crews around the country work diligently to prevent illegal narcotics from entering the United States.\n\nCoast Guard Cutter Kimball exemplified these operations during a recent patrol from February through April, during which they conducted multiple drug interdictions off the coasts of Mexico and Central and South America. This culminated in Kimball offloading more than $191 million worth of cocaine in April.\n\nAs the Coast Guard continues to surge assets across our southern border and maritime approaches, our crews have been leading the fight against drug cartels and Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCO). The dedicated efforts of Kimball – and men and women across the Coast Guard – are directly impacting the ability of cartels and TCOs to smuggle illicit drugs into our communities. \n\n📷PA3 Avery Tibbets & MST3 Austin Wiley\n\n@DHSgov @USCGPACAREA @USCGHawaiiPac \n\n#USCG #USCGHawaii #IndoPacific #druginterdiction",
