      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Strengthening partnerships to keep the American people safe! The crew of Coast Guard Cutter Robert Yered recently returned from a 28-day deployment around the Caribbean and Latin America.\n\nCGC Yered participated in the @ussouthcom exercise #Tradewinds25. Protecting global freedom of navigation keeps the American economy and people safe. That’s why Coast Guard crews foster regional cooperation with interagency partners and key allies.\n\nAnd Bravo Zulu to CGC Yered’s crew for being a winner in the coveted Coast Guard CDR Jim Simpson Public Affairs Awards! The CGC Yered earned first place for the 2024 Outstanding Unit Achievement Small Afloat. #USCG  #nationalsecurity #Partnership #oceansweek\n\n@USCGSoutheast @USCGLANTAREA @DHSgov  @DeptofDefense",
      "text_resolved": "Strengthening partnerships to keep the American people safe! The crew of Coast Guard Cutter Robert Yered recently returned from a 28-day deployment around the Caribbean and Latin America.\n\nCGC Yered participated in the @ussouthcom exercise #Tradewinds25. Protecting global freedom of navigation keeps the American economy and people safe. That’s why Coast Guard crews foster regional cooperation with interagency partners and key allies.\n\nAnd Bravo Zulu to CGC Yered’s crew for being a winner in the coveted Coast Guard CDR Jim Simpson Public Affairs Awards! The CGC Yered earned first place for the 2024 Outstanding Unit Achievement Small Afloat. #USCG  #nationalsecurity #Partnership #oceansweek\n\n@USCGSoutheast @USCGLANTAREA @DHSgov  @DeptofDefense",
